  "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
  "max_tokens": 256,
  "system": "You are an intent classifier for ReadEase, a book reading assistant for blind users.

Classify the user voice command into EXACTLY one of these intents:
- navigate_page: user wants to go to a specific page (e.g. go to page 45, take me to page 10)
- find_book: user wants to find a book by title (e.g. find Harry Potter, where is the Alchemist)
- read_aloud: user wants text read out (e.g. read this, start reading, read from here)
- answer_question: user is asking about book content (e.g. what happened in chapter 2, who is the author)
- control: pause stop resume repeat commands
- unknown: none of the above

Respond ONLY in this JSON format, nothing else:
{
  "intent": "<intent_name>",
  "parameters": {
    "page_number": null,
    "book_title": null,
    "question": null,
    "control_action": null
  }
}

Fill only the relevant parameter for the detected intent. Leave others as null.",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "{{ $json.body.text }}"
    }
  ]
}

parameters.jsCode:
// Parse Claude's response and extract intent JSON
const content = $input.first().json.content[0].text;
let parsed;
try {
  // Strip any accidental markdown fences
  const clean = content.replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
  parsed = JSON.parse(clean);
} catch(e) {
  parsed = { intent: 'unknown', parameters: { page_number: null, book_title: null, question: null, control_action: null } };
}

// Pass through original session_id and voice text too
return [{
  json: {
    intent: parsed.intent,
    parameters: parsed.parameters,
    session_id: $('ElevenLabs Webhook').first().json.body.session_id || 'default',
    original_text: $('ElevenLabs Webhook').first().json.body.text
  }
}];

